      "narrative": "The copper lamps flicker as you approach Mara Venn. She's leaning against the bar with a cup of something dark, her charcoal coat pulled tight against the morning chill. When you ask about the Ash Gate, her sharp eyes fix on you \u2014 and something flickers behind them. Wariness. Calculation.\n\nShe sets her cup down slowly.\n\n**Mara Venn:** \"The Ash Gate. That's a name I haven't heard spoken aloud in this tavern for a while.\" She tilts her head, studying you. \"Why's a knife-ear like you asking after a sealed door?\"\n\nThe word lands like a stone in still water. *Knife-ear.* A slur. She didn't stumble \u2014 she chose it. Testing you. Watching how you react.\n\nBefore you can respond, Toran Vex at the corner table flinches, ink-stained fingers freezing mid-scrawl. He doesn't look up, but his shoulders have gone tight as bowstrings.\n\nMara waits, one eyebrow raised. The question hangs \u2014 not about the Gate, but about *you*.\n\nWhat do you say?"
    },
