      "narrative": "Mara's eyes narrow at your question \u2014 then widen almost imperceptibly. The slur she threw at you hangs in the air, but your calm follow-up has shifted something. She wasn't expecting you to know about the lock at all.\n\nShe pushes off the bar, takes two steps closer. Her voice drops.\n\n**Mara Venn:** \"You know about the lock, do you?\" A beat. \"Toran Vex. That nervous little clerk with the ink-stained cuffs in the corner. He kept the Ash Gate's mechanism oiled and true for seven years. Sworn to the Kestrel Guild. Knew every pin, every spring, every whisper of that lock.\"\n\nShe jerks her chin toward Toran, who has gone very still at his table, quill frozen mid-air. A drop of ink falls from the nib, splattering on the wood.\n\n**Mara Venn:** \"Ask him yourself. If he'll talk.\" Her mouth twists. \"He hasn't touched that lock since the day it was filed shut. But he remembers every groove.\"\n\nShe watches you now \u2014 not with hostility, but with something closer to curiosity. The test is still there, but the edge has dulled.\n\nToran Vex doesn't look up, but his hand trembles slightly. He knows you're about to turn toward him.\n\nWhat do you do?"
    },
