      "narrative": "The copper lamps gutter as you lean in, pressing the question home. Mara's jaw tightens \u2014 she didn't expect you to push this far, this fast. For a long moment, she holds your gaze, weighing something behind those sharp eyes. Then she exhales through her nose, a sound almost like surrender.\n\n**Mara Venn:** \"Old Bram.\" She says the name flatly, as if it tastes of ash. \"The ferryman. He ran the passage for years \u2014 collected coin, turned the mechanism, let people through. Had his hand in the Kestrel Guild's pocket, and they had theirs in his.\"\n\nShe glances toward the shuttered window, toward where the Ash Gate stands beyond the rain-streaked glass.\n\n**Mara Venn:** \"Bram's dead now. Found him at the Gate three mornings ago. Throat cut, coin purse gone. Whoever filed the lock shut didn't want anyone following.\"\n\nShe turns back to you, arms crossed. Her voice drops lower.\n\n**Mara Venn:** \"That's the name you wanted. Old Bram. But he's not talking to anyone anymore.\"\n\nBehind you, a chair scrapes. Toran Vex has risen, his ink-stained hands pressed flat against his table, his face pale. He looks like a man deciding whether to bolt."
    },
