      "narrative": "Your voice cuts through the morning stillness, echoing off the narrow walls of the street.\n\n**\"Old Bram!\"**\n\nThe name ricochets down the cobbled lane, bounces off the cracked black arch, and fades into the heavy silence beyond. The crow on the keystone cocks its head, black eye fixed on you, but does not stir.\n\nNo answer comes.\n\nThe Ash Gate stands mute. The bloodstain at its base has darkened to a rusty brown, the edges feathered where rain has worked them thin. The air is cold and still, carrying only the distant creak of a sign swinging somewhere back toward the Copper Finch.\n\nNothing moves. Nothing answers.\n\nThe crow shifts its weight, clicks its beak once, and returns to watching you with patient, unblinking stillness.\n\nThe gate is sealed. The ferryman is dead. The street holds its breath around you.\n\nWhat do you do?"
